.SBTTL	OMEGA	The Omega changes to RT-11 V5.4
;
; Assembled after EDTGBL in every part of the monitor.  Each module is one
; architectural difference of the Omega SJ monitor from DEC's; it defines
; macros only, and DEC's sources call them where Omega changed them (the
; hooks are the patches of patches/series).
;
; Two builds come out of the same sources, told apart by OM$EXA, which
; the answers file (SYCND) sets:
;
;   OM$EXA = 1  Omega's monitor exactly - the reference, checked against
;               Omega's RT11SJ.SYS (SYCND.MAC);
;   OM$EXA = 0  DEC's RT-11 on the MS 0515: only what the machine needs,
;               DEC's own SYSGEN answers as far as the machine allows
;               (SYCDEC.MAC).  Omega's decoding trap, its NOP and HALT
;               filler and its repeated CONFIG bits are out.
;
; Omega's builds give two strings in Russian (OM$RUS, OMRUS.MAC); the dec
; profile keeps DEC's.
;
; A build can switch on the part only one Omega build has: OM$BLK, the
; vvv104 build's cursor blink through ROM-B (SYCOM2.MAC, profile omega2).
;
.IIF NDF OM$EXA, OM$EXA = 0
.IIF NDF OM$BLK, OM$BLK = 0
.IIF NDF OM$TRP, OM$TRP = 0
.IIF NDF OM$RUS, OM$RUS = 0
	.INCLUDE "SRC:OMTRAP.MAC"	;The decoding trap
	.INCLUDE "SRC:OMCONS.MAC"	;The console through the ROM
	.INCLUDE "SRC:OMCLOK.MAC"	;The clock: timer, floppy motor
	.INCLUDE "SRC:OMBOOT.MAC"	;The bootstrap on the MS 0515
	.INCLUDE "SRC:OMBLNK.MAC"	;The cursor blink through ROM-B
	.INCLUDE "SRC:OMRUS.MAC"	;Omega's two strings in Russian
